@page "/denied"
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization
@layout BareLayout
@attribute [AllowAnonymous]

@*
    Reached by somebody who is signed in and lacks the permission, so it is
    anonymous only in the sense that it must render without one — refusing
    access to the page that explains a refusal is a loop.
*@

<PageTitle>Not permitted — Jiranisoko Delivery</PageTitle>

<h1 class="bare__heading">Not permitted</h1>

<p>
    Your account is signed in, but it does not hold the permission this page
    needs. Nothing has gone wrong and there is nothing to retry.
</p>

<p>
    Permissions come with your role. If this is part of your work, ask an
    administrator to grant it — they can see exactly what is missing.
</p>

<p><a href="/">Back to your work</a></p>
